{"claims":[{"excerpt":"Uitgevouwen, maar nog niet klaar voor routinewetenschap","claim":"Webb being unfolded did not mean it was ready for routine science.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"After six months: “Science operations!” Webb began its science mission and started to conduct routine science operations.","narrative":"uitgevouwen zijn een belangrijke mijlpaal was, niet het einde van Webbs weg naar wetenschappelijke operaties.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source places routine science after the deployment and commissioning milestones.","materiality":"This distinction is the piece’s central point."},{"excerpt":"Webb moest opgevouwen in de kuip van de Ariane 5 passen: in zijn operationele configuratie was de telescoop daarvoor te groot.","claim":"Webb had to be folded to fit in the Ariane 5 fairing because its operational configuration was too large.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Webb's fully deployed operational configuration is far too large to fit into any available rocket so it was designed to fold into a compact launch configuration that fit inside the Ariane 5.","narrative":"Webb moest compact in de Ariane 5-raket passen, hoewel zijn operationele configuratie daarvoor te groot was.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source explicitly connects Webb’s size in its deployed configuration with its folded launch configuration.","materiality":"Provides accurate context for why deployment was necessary."},{"excerpt":"Het bereiken van die configuratie vereiste een uitvouwing met veel stappen en mogelijke faalpunten.","claim":"Reaching the operational configuration required a complex deployment with many steps and possible points of failure.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"There were over 50 major deployment steps, with 178 release mechanisms that had to perform perfectly or any one of over 300 single points of failure could have diminished or crippled the mission.","narrative":"De uitvouwing omvatte veel stappen en mogelijke faalpunten, waardoor duidelijk is dat dit een risicovolle fase was.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source documents numerous deployment steps and possible failure points.","materiality":"Conveys the complexity and stakes without claiming a failure occurred."},{"excerpt":"De uitvouwing verliep soepel.","claim":"Webb’s deployment proceeded smoothly.","category":"outcome","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Webb's deployment was completed with remarkable smoothness.","narrative":"de uitvouwing verliep soepel.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"This directly matches the source’s description.","materiality":"Clarifies that later commissioning work was not recovery from a deployment failure."},{"excerpt":"In de tweede week waren de spiegels uitgevouwen en vergrendeld.","claim":"By the second week, Webb’s mirror structures had been deployed and latched.","category":"technical","label":"F1 minor immaterial imprecision","evidence":"During the second week after launch, we finished deploying the telescope structures by unfolding and latching the secondary mirror tripod and rotating and latching the two primary mirror wings.","narrative":"In de tweede week waren de spiegels uitgevouwen en vergrendeld","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source specifies the secondary-mirror tripod and primary-mirror wings; “de spiegels” is a slightly broad shorthand for those structures.","materiality":"The simplification does not change the deployment timeline or outcome."},{"excerpt":"Webb had daarmee zijn operationele configuratie bereikt, maar was nog niet klaar voor routinewetenschap.","claim":"Webb had reached its fully deployed operational configuration, but was not yet ready for routine science.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"This brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration.","narrative":"De uitvouwing bracht de telescoop in de tweede week in die configuratie, maar was niet hetzelfde als klaar zijn voor routinewetenschap","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source distinguishes the second-week deployed configuration from the later start of routine science.","materiality":"This is the key distinction between deployment and operational readiness."},{"excerpt":"Tijdens de ingebruikname volgden weken van afkoeling, maanden van spiegeluitlijning en daarna de kalibratie van de instrumenten.","claim":"Commissioning included weeks of cooldown, months of mirror alignment, and then instrument calibration.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"In the first month: ... it took several weeks for them to cool all the way down and reach stable temperatures.","narrative":"afkoeling, spiegeluitlijning en instrumentkalibratie liepen door tijdens de ingebruikname van zes maanden.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source places cooldown in the first month, alignment in months two through four, and instrument calibration in months five and six.","materiality":"The sequence explains why deployment was not the endpoint."},{"excerpt":"Na zes maanden begon Webb aan routinewetenschap.","claim":"Webb began routine science after six months.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"After six months: “Science operations!” Webb began its science mission and started to conduct routine science operations.","narrative":"Na zes maanden begon Webb aan routinewetenschap.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The timing and outcome match the source.","materiality":"Establishes when routine operations began."},{"excerpt":"De uitvouwing was dus een belangrijke mijlpaal, maar niet het einde van de ingebruikname.","claim":"Deployment was an important milestone, but commissioning continued afterward.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"This brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration. ... The remaining five months of commissioning were all about aligning the optics and calibrating the scientific instruments.","narrative":"Daarmee maakt de tijdlijn het onderscheid duidelijk tussen de voltooide uitvouwing en het afronden van de ingebruikname.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source describes deployment as complete before the remaining commissioning activities and routine science operations.","materiality":"Summarizes the source-supported relationship between deployment and commissioning."}]}

